{"text": "To target 24 using the numbers [7, 7, 11, 12] with each number exactly once and using only the operations +, -, *, /, we need to find a combination that results in 24.", "start": 0, "end": 167, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Here's one way to achieve it:", "start": 168, "end": 197, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "First, consider the following steps:", "start": 199, "end": 235, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. Start with 12.", "start": 237, "end": 254, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Multiply by 7 (one of the 7s).", "start": 255, "end": 288, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Subtract 11.", "start": 289, "end": 304, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "4. Add the remaining 7.", "start": 305, "end": 328, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, the equation can be written as:", "start": 330, "end": 365, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "First, calculate 12 × 7:", "start": 386, "end": 410, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "12 × 7 = 84", "start": 411, "end": 422, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Next, subtract 11:", "start": 424, "end": 442, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "84 - 11 = 73", "start": 443, "end": 455, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Finally, add the remaining 7:", "start": 457, "end": 486, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "73 + 7 = 24", "start": 487, "end": 498, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Therefore, using the numbers 7, 7, 11, and 12, the expression to get 24 is:", "start": 500, "end": 575, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(12 × 7) - 11 + 7 = 24", "start": 576, "end": 598, "label": "inform"}
